    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d579">

                <pb facs="0558" n="550" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg550"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6623: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-01-08T18:00:00-05:00">January 8, 1941—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. Your 635, November 12, 1 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d579-f1"/> Please seek an
                    early occasion to discuss with the Foreign Minister<anchor n="2a"
                        xml:id="d579-f2"/> the situation at Tangier and recall to him the contents
                    of your note of November 11, 1940.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d579-f3"/> Point out
                    that although this Government is not a party to the Tangier Statute<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d579-f4"/> it not only has extensive rights in Morocco, based upon
                    treaties, custom and usage, but also, as an important naval power, it has an
                    inescapable interest in any developments taking place in Tangier which would be
                    likely to alter the neutral character of that port and district. Add that in
                    view of recent developments at Tangier, which your Government has observed with
                    some misgivings, the attention of the Spanish Government is again invited to the
                    above-mentioned American rights and interests in Tangier, in order that there
                    may be avoided any future misunderstanding which might hinder the progress of
                    those friendly relations which we are anxious to develop with Spain.</p>
                <p>Please leave with the Foreign Minister an <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi> in the sense of the foregoing and report the results of
                    your conversation by telegraph.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Tangier.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
